      "notes": "All four claims are well-supported by their quoted evidence. Tiers are correctly assigned: OBR projection is 'projected', goods export figure is 'measurable' from a cited source, stated claim is 'stated'. The too-uncertain direction correctly triggers n/a for magnitude and time_horizon. The crux_parameter and estimate_range are substantive, not lazy hedges. No lever leakage \u2014 the verdict judges effect on living standards/productivity, not the policy lever itself. No party identity or motive attribution detected. The mixed/uncertain verdict is genuinely backed by claims on both sides (downside: OBR productivity drag, EU resistance; upside: divergence proponents acknowledged). E34 source (export.org.uk) is media/trade body but is used only for the 'EU resistance' projected claim which is also corroborated by E33 (Commons Library, European Commission). No false balance \u2014 the rationale notes the institutional weight leans negative but the preparatory nature of the policy and genuine EU-response uncertainty justify too-uncertain. Verdict passes."
